# Leaning into Group Theory

Welcome to the Curriculum X 2026–27 course. These notes introduce interactive
theorem proving with Lean through examples and exercises in group theory.

Start with **Week 1** in the navigation menu. Read the explanations alongside
the Lean code; hover over code for more information and select a tactic to
inspect the proof state. To work through the examples yourself, open the
corresponding file in VS Code with the Lean extension.

## Intended learning outcomes

By the end of the course, you will be able to:

* Explain how an interactive theorem prover represents mathematical expressions,
  statements, and proofs.
* Identify the target, hypotheses, and goals at each stage of a proof.
* Prove group theory results using justified chains of equations and Lean's
  `calc` tactic.
* Distinguish forward and backward reasoning.
* Use `rw`, `apply`, `simp`, `show`, `change`, `have`, `intro`, `rcases`, and
  `use`, and explain how each changes a proof goal.
-/
